{%- comment -%}
  One field of hand-written prose from _data/*.yaml. Plain YAML strings, not markdown: escaped
  FIRST and transformed after, so the only markup an author can produce is <code> and a source
  marker, and a Rust generic like Array3<u8> survives as text.

  A shelf blurb is a YAML scalar and cannot include a template, so its sources hang off the section
  as data and the blurb carries bare `[1]` markers. The caller passes `prose_sources` and
  `prose_key`; both are cleared on the way out (Liquid `assign` is global -- see cratecard.liquid).
  A marker is replaced only when its number names a real source, so `[a]` and a bare `[` are left
  alone, and the pass runs per non-code chunk so a `[1]` inside `code` stays literal. It walks the
  sources backwards, or `[1]` would eat the first two characters of `[10]`.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- unless prose_sources -%}{%- assign prose_sources = "" -%}{%- endunless -%}
{%- unless prose_key -%}{%- assign prose_key = "" -%}{%- endunless -%}
{%- assign prose_nsrc = prose_sources | size -%}
{%- assign _parts = prose | escape | replace: "--", "—" | split: "`" -%}
{%- for _p in _parts -%}
{%- assign _odd = forloop.index0 | modulo: 2 -%}
{%- if _odd == 1 -%}<code>{{ _p }}</code>
{%- elsif prose_nsrc == 0 -%}{{ _p }}
{%- else -%}
{%- assign _marked = _p -%}
{%- assign _back = prose_sources | reverse -%}
{%- for _s in _back -%}
{%- assign _num = prose_nsrc | minus: forloop.index0 -%}
{%- capture _from -%}[{{ _num }}]{%- endcapture -%}
{%- capture _to -%}<a class="ref-mark" href="#src-{{ prose_key | escape }}-{{ _num }}"><span class="visually-hidden">Source </span><sup>{{ _num }}</sup><span class="visually-hidden">: {{ _s.src | escape }}</span></a>{%- endcapture -%}
{%- assign _marked = _marked | replace: _from, _to -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{{ _marked }}
{%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{%- assign prose_sources = "" -%}{%- assign prose_key = "" -%}
